			],
			"Message": "refactor(Element): Sync submodules with PascalCase naming convention\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with PascalCase refactoring:\n- Air: Rename CLI handlers (handle_status → Status, handle_restart → Restart, handle_config → Config, handle_metrics → Metrics, handle_logs → Logs, handle_debug → Debug) and plugin trait methods (handle_message → Message, handle_event → Event)\n- Grove: Rename handle_call → Call in APIBridgeImpl\n- Mountain: Rename IPC handler functions (handle_commands_execute → CommandsExecute, handle_configuration_get → ConfigurationGet, handle_incoming_message → IncomingMessage, etc.)\n- Sky: Add event-driven installation path for Wind's LandWorkbench bridge that listens for cel:services-ready, ensuring proper sequencing: services DI container populated → install Wind bridge → notify subscribers\n\nThese changes align with the project's naming convention specified in CLAUDE.md, removing handle_ prefixes for shorter, consistent method names across the codebase.",
			"SHA": "1d6badc56b52760aa91f3c847a1ae95c869aeb4a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:18:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				109,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Element): Batch command registration to eliminate IPC saturation during extension boot\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with coordinated performance fixes addressing keystroke lag during extension boot:\n- Mountain: Add CommandEmitBatch to buffer 1000+ registerCommand notifications and flush after 16ms, reducing individual emit storms to a single batched IPC round-trip\n- Output: Revert DisableLazyPaint opt-in gate (regressed editor mount) and remove PartZIndexCSS `isolation: isolate` rule that blocked input events under WKWebView\n- Sky: Accept batched `{ commands: [...] }` format alongside legacy single-command shape via new RegisterOneCommand helper\n- Cocoon: Sync to latest\n\nThese changes prevent 1000+ Tauri events per extension boot from saturating the shared WKWebView IPC channel that also delivers keystrokes, restoring input responsiveness during the most resource-intensive phase.\n\nRefs: Related to #10785a0 (IPC channel saturation), #9cae17e (lazy paint RAF/IO overrides)",
			"SHA": "ee7ae2629ee433d18040d6fd237bf9d2e1c28c70"
		}
